{"checks": {"bank": null, "dropped": 0, "drugs": true, "numbers": true, "redone": 0, "selfCheck": false, "shape": true, "verbatim": true}, "gen": "hand", "minutes": 8, "module": "ssg-peritoneal-surface-malignancy", "quiz": [], "refs": ["Sabiston Surgery 22e Ch 70, peritoneum", "PSOGI Consensus 2022", "PSOGI Pseudomyxoma guideline 2022", "PRODIGE 7 trial", "OVHIPEC trial"], "src": ["ss-c-peritoneal-ground"], "steps": [{"say": "The peritoneal cancer index scores thirteen abdominopelvic regions zero to three for lesion size, with totals over twenty marking extensive disease. Complete cytoreduction is unlikely above twenty, so the score decides operability. Score every region at staging laparoscopy.", "tx": "**Peritoneal cancer index** scores **13** abdominopelvic regions **0** to **3** for lesion size, with total over **20** of 39 marking extensive disease where complete **cytoreduction** is unlikely. Extensive small bowel and mesenteric involvement weighs heaviest against completeness, since these areas cannot be stripped safely. Document the score on a standard grid so centres compare cases honestly.", "vis": {"cols": ["PCI band", "Meaning", "Decision"], "kind": "table", "rows": [["Under 15", "Limited disease", "CRS plus HIPEC"], ["15 to 20", "Borderline", "Select carefully"], ["Over 20", "Extensive", "Unlikely complete"]]}},
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     {
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      "tx": "The **peritoneal cancer index** gives each of thirteen abdominopelvic regions a score from 0 to 3 for lesion size. The maximum total is 39, and a total above 20 marks extensive disease in which complete cytoreduction is unlikely. Disease on the small bowel and mesentery weighs most against a complete clearance, because those surfaces cannot be stripped safely. Writing every region on a standard grid lets centres compare cases honestly instead of calling the abdomen merely widespread.",
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      "say": "Thirteen peritoneal regions are scored 0 to 3 for lesion size. A total above 20 out of 39 means extensive disease and makes a complete cytoreduction unlikely. Small bowel and mesenteric deposits argue most strongly against stripping every surface. The score belongs on a standard grid.",
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      "vis": {
