                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     }, {"say": "Completeness of cytoreduction decides HIPEC benefit. CC zero with no visible disease and CC one under two point five millimetres gain from heated chemotherapy, while CC two or three debulking without HIPEC is avoided. Incomplete surgery plus HIPEC helps no one.", "tx": "**Completeness of cytoreduction** CC-**0** with no visible disease and CC-**1** at **2.5** mm or less decide **HIPEC** benefit, and CC-**2** or CC-**3** debulking without HIPEC is avoided. Chemotherapy penetrates only millimetres, so visible nodules left behind waste the heated perfusion. Record completeness photographically, since the score is among the strongest predictors of survival.", "vis": {"edges": [["small", "cc01"], ["cc01", "hipec"], ["bulky", "systemic"]], "kind": "flow", "nodes": [{"id": "small", "label": "Resectable to CC-0/1"}, {"id": "cc01", "label": "Complete CRS"}, {"id": "hipec", "label": "Add HIPEC"}, {"id": "bulky", "label": "Only CC-2/3 possible"}, {"id": "systemic", "label": "Systemic therapy"}]}}, {"say": "Pseudomyxoma from ruptured appendiceal mucinous neoplasm typically gets complete cytoreduction with mitomycin HIPEC at forty two degrees for ninety minutes in a common protocol. Ten year survival exceeds sixty percent with complete surgery for low-grade disease. Refer to a peritoneal centre before the first incision.", "tx": "**Pseudomyxoma peritonei** from ruptured appendiceal mucinous neoplasm typically gets complete CRS with **mitomycin** HIPEC at **42** degrees for **90** minutes in a common protocol, with **10**-year survival over **60** percent. Low-grade jelly spreads along peritoneal fluid paths to the omentum and hemidiaphragms, sparing the small bowel serosa early. Peritonectomy of involved parietal surfaces plus omentectomy achieves CC-0 in experienced hands.", "vis": {"cols": ["Disease", "HIPEC drug", "Outcome"], "kind": "table", "rows": [["Pseudomyxoma", "Mitomycin, 42 C, 90 min", "Over 60% at 10 years"], ["Mesothelioma", "Cisplatin-based", "Epithelioid best"], ["Colorectal (trials)", "Oxaliplatin or mitomycin", "Select PCI under 15"]]}}, {"say": "Colorectal peritoneal metastases with PCI under fifteen and no extraperitoneal disease get CRS with HIPEC in trials, while PRODIGE seven showed no HIPEC add on benefit. Cytoreduction itself still helps selected patients. Enrol in trials rather than assuming HIPEC adds value.", "tx": "**Colorectal peritoneal metastases** with PCI under **15** as a selection guide and no extraperitoneal disease get CRS, with HIPEC a trial question,, while **PRODIGE** **7** showed oxaliplatin HIPEC added no survival benefit. Complete resection drives the survival gain, and HIPEC adds morbidity without proven extra months in this group. Offer CRS for limited resectable disease and honest counselling about the HIPEC question.", "vis": {"kind": "compare", "left": {"points": ["PCI under 15", "No extra spread", "CRS, trial HIPEC"], "title": "Limited: operate"}, "right": {"points": ["PCI over 20", "Liver plus lung spread", "Systemic therapy"], "title": "Extensive: do not"}}}, {"say": "Diffuse malignant peritoneal mesothelioma with epithelioid histology and BAP1 loss suits CRS with cisplatin HIPEC, while sarcomatoid disease gets systemic therapy. Histology writes the plan here. Biphasic disease individualises toward trials.", "tx": "Diffuse malignant peritoneal **mesothelioma** with **epithelioid** histology suits CRS with cisplatin HIPEC, while sarcomatoid and biphasic disease get systemic therapy. Asbestos exposure history supports the diagnosis, and BAP1 immunostain loss favours malignancy over reactive proliferation. Complete parietal and visceral peritonectomy with heated cisplatin gives the best chance of long-term survival in epithelioid disease.", "vis": {
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                